# Stages core.ts runs that no system tree describes yet.
#
# check-atlas.sh requires every stage to be either in a tree or listed here, so the atlas cannot
# quietly fall behind the pipeline: a NEW stage fails the build until somebody decides which
# system it belongs to. A line here is an admission, not an exemption — the list shrinks as the
# atlas is built and its length is the honest measure of how far along it is.
#
# Written 2026-09-03 with corporate credit as the only mapped system. The domain half was added
# when the gate was extended to src/domain: the README had claimed that coverage and the script
# had never checked it, so 72 modules were invisible to the instrument built to find absences.

